# The CI test image, ghcr.io/jkkelley/coq-test: what every shell-family suite (herdr, factory, line, events, loop, sitrep, scheduler-host,
# reindex) runs in as a Kubernetes pod container, without podman on the host or in the pod (WO-20261013-8573, design
# 20261013194800-ci-gate-design.md, amendment 20:04Z). Build it with ci/image/build.sh, never by hand: the base digest, the herdr version and
# its checksums are read from ci/config/images.json, so no script and no Containerfile carries a second copy of them.
#
# BREADCRUMB 2026-10-13 - WO-20261013-8573. What broke (found while writing this image): herdr/tests/Containerfile pins its base to
#   debian@sha256:520c7157..., which is a single linux/amd64 manifest, and the suite bind-mounts the host's static x86-64 herdr
#   (herdr/tests/run.sh). The cluster is arm64 (k8s-worker-01/02 and the control plane are Raspberry Pis), so that image would die with
#   'exec format error' on the first exec, as the lint image did on 2026-10-10 (lint/Containerfile header), and a pod has no host binary to bind-mount.
#   Why this fix: the base is the multi-arch INDEX digest of debian:stable-slim (pinned by digest, Rule 15), and herdr is baked in from its
#   release page per architecture and checked against the sha256 in images.json, so the suite tests the exact release the fleet runs (0.9.0) on
#   either architecture. Rejected: one amd64 image under qemu in the cluster (slow, and a herdr server under emulation is not what the fleet runs)
#   and a bind-mounted host binary (a pod has no host). Cost: a herdr bump is a version and two checksums in images.json plus a new image tag.
#
# Repin the base deliberately (index digest, not the per-platform one `podman image inspect` prints):
#   curl -sI -H 'Accept: application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json' -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
#     https://registry-1.docker.io/v2/library/debian/manifests/stable-slim | grep -i docker-content-digest
ARG BASE
FROM ${BASE}
ARG TARGETARCH
ARG HERDR_VERSION
ARG HERDR_SHA256_AMD64
ARG HERDR_SHA256_ARM64
RUN apt-get update -qq \
  && apt-get install -y -qq --no-install-recommends bash jq git python3 python3-jsonschema ca-certificates procps ncurses-bin curl make shellcheck libxml2-utils >/dev/null \
  && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
RUN case "$TARGETARCH" in \
      amd64) arch=x86_64; sha="$HERDR_SHA256_AMD64" ;; \
      arm64) arch=aarch64; sha="$HERDR_SHA256_ARM64" ;; \
      *) echo "coq-test: no herdr build for $TARGETARCH" >&2; exit 1 ;; \
    esac \
  && curl -fsSL --retry 3 -o /usr/local/bin/herdr "https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr/releases/download/v${HERDR_VERSION}/herdr-linux-${arch}" \
  && echo "${sha}  /usr/local/bin/herdr" | sha256sum -c - \
  && chmod 0755 /usr/local/bin/herdr
RUN git config --system user.email "coq-tests@example.invalid" \
  && git config --system user.name "coq seat suite" \
  && git config --system --add safe.directory "*" \
  && git config --system init.defaultBranch main
